**Council guidance on outbuildings:** Garden rooms and sheds generally don't need a planning application if they meet all of these conditions:
- No more than 2.5 metres high
- Behind the front wall of the house
- Covering less than half the garden

If your design meets all three, it probably doesn't need an application. If it doesn't, or if you're unsure, you should apply. I can't give a formal planning opinion, so please confirm with the planning team before you start work. [withheld] development rights can also be removed by conditions on earlier permissions, so it's worth checking the property's planning history.

